lesson k-my-body-and-senses v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=7 subject=nature levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "My body and my senses"
  goal "Name the parts of the body we sense with, say which one is used for each sense, and count parts of the body."

  look {
    scene 7x9 {
      person ada pose=wave age=child hair=bunches colour=black top=berry at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
      We find out about the world with our senses. We see with our eyes, hear with our ears, smell
      with our nose, taste with our tongue and feel with our skin. Our eyes need light: in the dark
      there is nothing to see by.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.which-sense k=0 level=medium
    }
    practice k.which-sense count=3 seed=2 easy-count=2
    show k.count-fingers side="right" hard-side="both"
    practice k.body-count count=2 seed=3
    show k.see-by-light l=1
    show k.sense-and-say
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.dark-room
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.senses-at-once k=1 hard-k=0
  }
  remember {
    say "Eyes see, ears hear, nose smells, tongue tastes, and skin feels."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Read each question aloud, and let the child point to the part of their own body. Skin as the
    sense of touch is the one children forget, since they think of hands. The listening question is
    for you to hear. If the child is stuck on the dark room, go into a dark cupboard together and
    see how little you can see. Off the page, play a feely bag game and a smell game with lemon and
    mint. China, 3-6岁儿童学习与发展指南 (learning and development guide for children aged 3 to 6),
    科学探究 (recalled, not fetched): "能用多种感官或动作去探索物体" (Explore objects with several
    senses and movements.)
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level smelling is worked in the teacher's pen first, the senses are smell, hearing and sight, one hand is counted, and the three-star cat uses three senses."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the senses include taste and a smell that warns, both hands are counted, and the three-star apple uses four senses."
  }
}
